Source: coolprop
Section: libs
Priority: optional
Maintainer: CoolProp developers <coolprop@coolprop.org>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13),
               cmake (>= 3.14),
               g++,
               pkg-config,
               python3 (>= 3.9),
               libeigen3-dev (>= 3.4),
               libfmt-dev
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Homepage: https://www.coolprop.org
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: libcoolprop8
Section: libs
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: thermophysical property library for fluids and humid air
 CoolProp implements pure and pseudo-pure fluid equations of state and
 transport properties for 122 components, mixture properties using
 high-accuracy Helmholtz energy formulations, correlations of incompressible
 fluids and brines, and psychrometric routines for humid air.
 .
 This package contains the shared library.  The fluid data is compiled into
 the binary, so there is no separate data package and nothing to configure at
 runtime.
 .
 Note on dependencies: the library calls dlopen(), which needs no explicit
 dependency because libc6 provides it and ${shlibs:Depends} picks that up.
 The 2014 packaging attempt listed a package called "dl" here, which does not
 exist and made the package uninstallable.

Package: libcoolprop-dev
Section: libdevel
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: libcoolprop8 (= ${binary:Version}),
         ${misc:Depends},
         libeigen3-dev,
         libfmt-dev
Description: thermophysical property library for fluids and humid air (development)
 CoolProp implements pure and pseudo-pure fluid equations of state and
 transport properties for 122 components, mixture properties using
 high-accuracy Helmholtz energy formulations, correlations of incompressible
 fluids and brines, and psychrometric routines for humid air.
 .
 This package contains the headers, the pkg-config file and the CMake package
 configuration.  Use <CoolProp/CoolProp.h> for the C++ API or
 <CoolProp/CoolPropLib.h> for the C API.
 .
 The C++ headers are not self-contained: they include Eigen and fmt, hence the
 dependencies on libeigen3-dev and libfmt-dev.  See README.md in
 dev/packaging/ for the version-skew caveat that comes with that.
